    "story": "His hand is up at his helmet because the noise has not stopped long enough for him to think, and the thinking is the part of the job that doesn't show. The rifle is heavy on the strap, the dust is in his throat, and the ground ahead is broken and empty all the way to the far tree line. He has stopped walking because walking without knowing what is ahead is how a man gets himself killed, and the hand stays up while he listens for whatever the quiet is hiding.",
