    "title": "The Paper by the Fire",
    "description": "A woman in a red snood and a pale blue dress sits in an armchair by a fireplace, reading a newspaper whose headline reports the D-Day landings, a framed photograph of a young soldier on the mantel beside a radio. The painterly color treatment keeps the frame in warm, domestic tones — the dark wood of the mantel, the red of the snood, and the soft light of the room all holding the same muted, late-afternoon glow.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame is a portrait of the war as it reaches a living room — one woman, one newspaper, and a photograph that never leaves the mantel.\n\nShe reads the headline a third time.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
    "alt": "A painterly color photograph of a World War II home-front scene: a woman in a red snood and pale blue dress sitting in an armchair by a fireplace reading a newspaper about the D-Day landings, a framed photograph of a young soldier on the mantel beside a radio. Painterly fine art photography, World War II, Facing History.",
    "buyLink": "https://wayne-heim.smugmug.com/Galleries/Painterly-Fine-Art-Photography/Facing-History/WWII/War/Color/i-nrtRrhM/A",

