    "story": "Low tide leaves the beach honest. Whatever the night brought in — a mine, a boat, a man — is lying out there in the wet sand waiting to be found, and finding it before it finds a fisherman is the whole of the morning's work. Two rifles. A long walk to where the ground ends. The lighthouse kept the night watch out here so they wouldn't have to; now it's their turn to walk its watch back.",
