    "description": "Two German soldiers in camouflage smocks and steel helmets stand as lookouts by a wooden log wall, one standing and gesturing with his hand raised, the other seated with his rifle, a basket of apples and a bottle on a stone ledge beside them. The painterly color treatment keeps the frame in warm, village tones — the mottled log wall, the camouflage fabric, and the dark metal of the rifles all holding the same muted afternoon light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame is a study in a warning given quietly — two men, one hand in the air, and a street that has gone still.\n\nThe warning is given, and the street goes quiet.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
