    "description": "An American soldier in a netted steel helmet and olive drab uniform kneels behind a steel hedgehog anti-tank obstacle on a sandy beach, his rifle held upright in both hands, another soldier partially visible behind him. The painterly color treatment keeps the frame in pale, sandy tones — the steel of the obstacle, the olive uniform, and the pale sky all holding the same flat, sun-bleached light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame is a study in cover that was never meant for a man — the hedgehog built for tanks, and the soldier borrowing it for a morning.\n\nHe stays low until the beach gives him a reason to move.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
