    "title": "What's our next move?",
    "description": "Two American soldiers lie prone in the sand on a Normandy beach, rifles down beside them, steel hedgehogs rising all around them in the pale light. The man in front grins toward the camera while the man beside him looks off to the right, and more men crouch behind them in the haze. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the sand, the khaki uniforms, and the netted helmets all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame catches the long minute under fire, when men lie low, keep their rifles close, and grin at the camera like the beach is not trying to kill them.\n\nThe hedgehogs stay where they are, and the sand stays under the men, and the next move is still to be made.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
