    "description": "An American soldier in a steel helmet and full field gear runs across open ground, his rifle held across his chest and his pack bouncing on his back, his eyes fixed ahead and his mouth open with the effort. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the olive drab of his uniform, the worn leather of the rifle sling, and the pale, hazy backdrop all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame catches the run itself, the moment when a man with everything he owns on his back has to cover open ground and cover it fast.\n\nThe trees are still ahead, and the run is still going.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
