    "description": "An American soldier in a netted steel helmet holds an M1 rifle diagonally across his body, his eyes lifted toward something above and beyond the frame. The painterly color treatment holds the portrait in warm, muted tones — the tan of his uniform, the worn wood of the rifle, and the pale, textured backdrop all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame is a portrait first and a battle frame second: the rifle held close, the eyes already somewhere else.\n\nThe rifle stays across his body, and his eyes stay up, and the frame stays on the looking.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
