    "story": "Every infantryman learns the sky is a road, and traffic on it is never good news. The sound came first — it always does — a note in the air his grandfather would have taken for weather. His eyes went up the way a hand goes up in church: without asking the rest of him. Down here, the field can be read. Up there, a man just listens with his eyes and waits to find out what the road is bringing.",
    "notes": "This one hangs best at eye level, because the man in it is not looking at you — he is looking past you, up and out of the frame, and every person who walks by will follow his eyes to the ceiling. The rifle lies diagonal across his chest like a bar across a door, and the netted helmet and the tan uniform sit warm in the painterly color. Hang it where the room is quietest, and let the man's eyes do the talking.",
