    "description": "An American soldier runs across a beach battlefield, his rifle high in one hand and his pack on his back, leaning into the run as other soldiers advance behind him and a fallen man lies on the sand. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the sand, the khaki uniforms, and the hazy sky all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the charge in mid-step — the rifle up, the sand flying, the beach open ahead and the fallen man behind.\n\nThe run goes on, and the men behind him go on with it.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
