    "story": "The man behind him is not getting up. That's the whole briefing. Whatever the plan was this morning, it's down to this: the beach doesn't shorten, the open doesn't close, and the only direction the day still offers is forward, one long step at a time. He doesn't decide it so much as hear it — the voice a man uses on himself when there's nobody left to give the order. Move. Then move again. The second order is the harder one.",
    "notes": "Charge pictures are usually lies — all momentum, no cost. This one keeps its cost in the frame: a man down on the sand behind the runner, and the runner still going. That's the brag a collector can make about it — the exact transaction the war demanded, a life spent and the line still moving, inside a single stride. Collectors put it where they introduce the room to the set, because after this frame nobody asks whether the work is serious.",
