    "story": "They are walking and they are talking, and the talking carries them farther than the walking does, because a man can carry his pack for miles but he cannot carry the quiet for miles, and the quiet is heavier than the pack. The rifles are slung loose over their shoulders and the packs are on their backs and the field is open in front of them, and the words between them are about the place they came from, not the place they are going, and home comes up more than any other word, and home carries them farther than their feet do.",
