    "description": "An American medic in a steel helmet marked with red crosses bends over a wounded soldier lying flat on the ground, his hand on the man's chest and his medical pack still on his back, an American flag patch on his sleeve and a concrete post at the edge of the frame. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the khaki uniform, the red of the crosses, and the grey of the concrete all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the medic's hardest minute: the hand on the chest, the face bent close, and the man on the ground still.\n\nThe hand stays on his chest, and the medic stays bent over him, and the ground stays still.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
    "alt": "A painterly color photograph of an American World War II medic in a steel helmet marked with red crosses bending over a wounded soldier lying on the ground, his hand on the man's chest, his medical pack on his back. Painterly fine art photography, World War II, Facing History.",
