    "description": "An American sergeant with three chevrons on his sleeve laughs in a snowy forest, a BAR held across his arms and leather gloves on his hands, his helmet netted against the trees and other soldiers moving through the snow behind him. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the khaki uniform, the brown leather of the gloves, and the pale snow all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the laugh in the snow: the sergeant, the BAR, and the cold that does not stop him from laughing.\n\nThe snow stays on the trees, and the laugh stays on his face, and the column stays behind him.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
