    "description": "An American soldier in a steel helmet aims his rifle straight toward the camera, his cheek against the stock and his eye down the sights, the barrel pointing out of the frame while another soldier crouches below him. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the tan of his uniform, the worn wood of the rifle, and the mottled backdrop all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the aiming itself: the rifle up, the eye down the sights, and the ground past the camera still holding whatever he is looking at.\n\nThe barrel stays pointed out, and the eye stays down the sights, and the man below stays crouched.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
