    "story": "Two men, two theologies of wire. One goes under it, cheek in the dirt, trusting the earth. One goes over it, trusting the air and his own legs. The wire doesn't care which gospel a man picks — it charges the same toll either way, in time, in noise, in skin. And the cover they're running for is, at this moment, mostly a rumor: a fold in the ground somebody said was there. Men have crossed worse on thinner promises. The wire keeps the change.",
    "notes": "One frame, two answers to the same problem — a man under the wire and a man over it, caught in the same second. That's the claim a collector can make: it isn't a picture of a crossing, it's a picture of choice, and guests pick their man and argue about it. Pictures that start arguments between guests are the ones that never come down.",
