    "title": "Guys We Got to Do Something",
    "description": "American soldiers take cover behind a steel hedgehog on a beach, rifles up and packs on their backs, one laughing in the middle of the group while others watch the ground and the sky. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the sand, the khaki uniforms, and the dark steel of the hedgehog all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the pinned-down minute: the steel in front, the rifles up, and a laugh going on while the men plan the move out of it.\n\nThe hedgehog stays where it is, and the men stay behind it, and the laugh stays on.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
    "alt": "A painterly color photograph of American World War II soldiers taking cover behind a steel hedgehog on a beach, rifles up, one laughing in the middle of the group while others watch the ground and the sky. Painterly fine art photography, World War II, Facing History.",
