    "story": "A firing line is a machine for saying no. No — this ground is occupied. No — you will not walk across it upright. Each man fires into the same argument, and between the shots the line breathes together, works bolts together, spends the same smoke. Alone, a rifleman is a target with opinions. Shoulder to shoulder on the line, the same men become weather — something the other side has to plan around, dress for, and finally wait out.",
    "notes": "A firing line, caught at the moment it stops being men and becomes a position. The brag a collector can make: this is the set's wall picture — shoulder to shoulder, smoke still hanging from the last volley, a rhythm you can almost hear — and it anchors a room the way the line anchored its ground. Guests who know rifles linger here longest, reading the line the way the men held it.",
