    "description": "American soldiers move in a tight cluster on a beach, one shouting with his mouth wide open and his hands out while the men on either side of him hold his arms, sandbags piled behind them and rifles across their backs. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the sand, the khaki uniforms, and the dark metal of the rifles all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the shout itself: the mouth open, the hands on his arms, and the whole cluster moving as one.\n\nThe shout stays open, and the hands stay on his arms, and the sandbags stay behind them.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
