    "story": "The ground went first. Not under fire. Not dramatic. Just sand, giving way under a boot that had trusted it a second too long. The pack pulled him backwards, the rifle stayed in his hand because his hand had forgotten how to let go, and the world tilted — sky, sand, sky again. He could hear his own breath, loud, and somebody shouting his name from above, and the sea, still there, still indifferent. He thought, absurdly, of a hill at home, a sledge, a winter afternoon when falling had been a game. This was not that. And yet the body remembered how to fall, and how to roll, and how to get up again, and somewhere in the middle of it all he understood that getting up was the whole of it.",
