    "story": "A hand at his back. Not a shove. Not a grip. A hand — flat, firm, saying, this way. That was how it started. The smoke was thinning. The shouting had dropped to single words, names, directions. He kept his hands up because his hands were a sentence anyone could read. The ground was soft under his boots. The pack of the man behind him brushed his shoulder. Somewhere, far off, a bird was singing, and the sound of it was so ordinary it hurt. He thought of a road home, and of how long it was, and of whether it would still be there when he got to it. He did not know. He knew the hand at his back. He knew the next step. And for now, that was enough to walk with.",
