    "story": "How far to the hedgehogs? He did not know. Nobody did. The road was wider than it had looked from the ditch, and the rifle in his hands felt solid, and that was something. The man behind him was shouting — his name, or a direction, or both at once — and the sound folded into the thump of boots on the dirt track. The prone man in the middle distance had gone still in the way men go still when they are listening for something they cannot see. He kept running. The pack pulled at his shoulders. The air tasted of dust and diesel and rain that had not yet fallen. He thought of a road at home, a lane between hedges, a bicycle leaning against a gate — and the thought came and went so fast he barely caught it. Ahead, the trees were grey. Ahead, the ground rose. Ahead, the next few yards, and then the ones after that, and then — he did not let himself finish it. He ran.",
