    "story": "They had been walking together since the boat. Not friends, exactly — not yet — but a pair, the way the army makes pairs out of strangers, and the way strangers become something else on a road like this one. He watched the other man's step, and the other man watched his, and between them they kept a rhythm that neither of them could have kept alone. The hedgehogs in the field were the first thing that looked like it belonged to this war — iron, black, waiting — and he gave them a wide berth in his mind, and then in his feet. The air was cold and damp. The pack was a weight, and the rifle was a weight, and the road was a weight, and still the two of them kept going, because there was a field, and a hedge, and a village nobody had named yet, and because turning back had stopped being a direction.",
