    "story": "It happened in the space of a breath. One foot on the mound, the next already past it, and the ground falling away behind him like something he had only borrowed. The rifle was up, and then it was not, and then it was up again, because his hands had decided before his head had caught up. Below, in the earth, a man lay still in the dirt, and he kept his own eyes on the top of the mound — on the getting over, on the second man beside him counting on the same breath. The beret at the edge of the frame was a face he could half-see, and it was enough: somebody else was here, somebody else was moving, and the whole thing was not his alone to carry. The air was thick with dust and the smell of turned earth. He cleared the top. The ground on the other side rose to meet him, and he went down into it without looking back, because looking back was a place for later, when there was time to be afraid of what he had seen.",
