    "story": "You ready? The question hung between them, unasked, and it did not need asking. The young man in profile had it written across his face — the set of his jaw, the way his eyes stayed on the other man's helmet and the red diamond painted on it. A five. His five, now — the one he would follow when the ramp dropped and the water took the shouting away. Follow the five, whatever else came apart. Follow the five. The other man had his back to the camera, and his back said more than his face ever could: the pack, the straps, the helmet, the whole weight of the crossing, carried without a word. Behind them, the rest of the craft stood the same way — close, quiet, under a sky that had not yet shown its hand. A morning tried to surface — a kitchen, ordinary light — and went under. The man in front of him was turning. The turning was the signal. And the signal was already moving.",
