    "story": "A red scarf. In daylight. He knew what it made of him — a flag walking — and he had stopped arguing with it two villages back. It had been knotted by hands that were not his, in a doorway, with instructions: come back wearing it. So he wore it. The glasses kept misting at the edges; he had learned to aim through the clear middle and trust the rest. Bent double, the world came down to boots and dust and the Sten's sling biting his shoulder. Whatever crossed the road ahead would cross it in front of a man who looked ridiculous and shot straight. He intended to be both.",
    "notes": "After the jeep frame, this is the pairing that makes the set — the same resistance fighter, bending low, the scarf the only color the morning gives. Collectors who take the jeep frame will want this one beside it: the portrait of the man, not the vehicle, a tight profile a collector can hang in a study or a hall and point to when the conversation turns to the men who walked bent low through a war that gave them no uniforms.",
