    "story": "Drive, when the word comes. Not before. His hands sat at ten and two like a schoolboy's, and the gun across his lap made the posture a lie — nobody drives to church with a rifle for a seatbelt. Behind him, out in the haze, the other one watched the treeline and said nothing, which was the arrangement: one pair of eyes for the road, one for everything that wasn't the road. The engine idled rough. It had idled rough since the drop, and rough had started to sound like reliable. When the word came it would be a word, not a shout. He kept his foot off the pedal and his boot ready, and the haze kept whatever it was keeping.",
