    "story": "From where she hung, the world was a shoulder, a strap, and a patch: an eagle, white on black, going up and down with his breath. She counted the breaths because counting was a thing her mind could still do without asking her body's permission. Below the eagle, the road went past in pieces — dust, a boot, dust again. She had been carried twice in her life before: by her father, through a fair crowd, and once out of a river, coughing. Both times she had been small enough to make it easy. This time she held on like cargo that knew its own weight, and kept her eyes on the eagle, and let it carry her eyes the way he carried the rest.",
