    "story": "Inside the hull, the tank was all engine. Out of the hatch, the world came back — wind, birdsong, a field so green it looked unconsulted. He rode with his elbows on the rim and the headphones half on, one ear for the set, one for the morning, because orders travel by wire but trouble usually announces itself out loud. Behind him the gunner kept the big gun company. Below, in the belly, the driver waited for a word that would travel down through his boot. Three men, one machine, and a road that had not yet decided what it was. He flexed his fingers on the rim. \"Easy,\" he said, to nobody, to everybody. The tank breathed under him like something asleep with one eye open.",
