    "story": "The blast did not push him. It took the ground's side away — one moment the trench had a floor he trusted, the next the floor was a rumour and his arms were out doing the old, stupid mathematics of falling. His ears rang at a pitch no bird ever made. Dirt came down out of a sky that had been empty a second before, rattling on his helmet like weather. Behind him, flat on the bank, the other one kept his rifle level and his head down, a whole education in one posture. He got a foot under him. Then the other. Standing, when it comes back, does not feel like victory. It feels like being allowed to continue.",
