    "story": "The dust was the country now. It had eaten the road, the sky, the second man — no, there he was, a shape in the brown, keeping the distance the way they both had been taught: close enough to matter, far enough to survive the same shell. His rifle rode slung and slapping, an annoyance he would have missed if it stopped. Run where? Forward was a direction the dust still permitted. His mouth tasted of the road he was running on, grit between the teeth, and his lungs had started their negotiation: less air, they offered, or slower legs. He declined both. Somewhere ahead the dust would thin, because dust always thins. He ran toward the rumour of it.",
