    "story": "You walk past them one at a time. The hedgehogs. Big as gateposts, iron, stupid. Nothing wheeled gets past them. You are not wheeled. You walk. The pack is heavy. The rifle is heavier. The man on the ground beside the first hedgehog is not moving. You look at him. You do not stop. There is no stopping here. The haze eats the men ahead of you. It eats the men behind you too. The hedgehogs stay. They always stay. And the man on the ground — you look at him once more. Then you look away, and keep walking.",
