    "story": "'Go!' The word came from behind him. His legs answered before his mind did. Dust. Dust in his eyes, dust in his mouth, dust on the rifle, dust everywhere except the road ahead, and the road ahead was clear. He ran with the rifle clutched across his chest, both hands on it, knuckles white. The man on the ground behind him fired once, at the hedge, or the hedgehog, or nothing at all. He did not turn to look. The hedgehog stood in the road like a piece of the road that had grown teeth. The men behind him were coming, boots on the dirt. He ran. The road ran with him. And then the road went quiet.",
