    "story": "The beach smelled of salt and cordite and diesel. The pack on his back was heavy. It had been heavy since the ramp went down. The tank behind him crept forward, slow, through the sand. The man lying prone at the left did not move. He did not move at all. The hedgehogs stood in the sand like the teeth of a jaw that had forgotten how to close. He ran. The radio on his back stayed silent. It had not spoken since the ramp went down. He lifted the handset. He put it to his mouth. He said: 'Through.'",
