    "story": "He had known the man on the ground since the boat. They had shared a blanket on the boat. The blanket was thin. They had joked about freezing before they ever got shot. The joke was not funny now. The man on the ground was not laughing. He lay with one arm out, palm up. The tank behind him idled. He could hear the idling, low, through the dust. His throat was full of dust. He had not touched his canteen since the morning. He looked down at the hand. The hand was still. He reached for it. His fingers stopped an inch short.",
