    "story": "He dropped to his knees beside the man in the sandbags. The sandbags were still warm from the sun. The sun was low. Low sun made long shadows, and the smoke softened every one. Somewhere behind them, in the smoke, the tank was still running. He pressed his palm to the man's chest. The chest rose. The rise was shallow. He said the man's name. The name did not come back to him. The man opened his eyes. They found his face. He did not look away. He stayed. Would the line hold? Nobody in the smoke knew.",
    "notes": "The kneeling man is the composition — the smoke, the sandbags, the tank all making room around him. Collectors who own the tank frames will want this one for the staying: the man who did not move on. In a Facing History grouping it hangs as the image that stops a visitor mid-step, and the man still kneeling is why.",
