    "story": "Left, right. Left, right. His boots found the rhythm before his mind did. The firing came from his left, three rounds at a time. The prone man worked the trigger. The trigger answered. The pole rode on his shoulder. He had practised this weight on flat ground, and the ground here was not flat. The sandbags were soft under his boots. He stepped over the last one. His foot came down in dust. The dust rose. His boots hit the dust, and the dust answered with a sound like paper tearing.",
