    "story": "The tank could not cross the sandbags. So he went over them himself. The ground left his boots. The sandbags went under him. He was in the air for one whole second. The second stretched. The tank was behind him, growling in the smoke. He kept his rifle close to his chest. His hands were cold on the grip. The grip was wet with sweat. The sweat had been there since the run. The run had started at the trees. He had not looked back at the trees. His boots found the ground on the other side.",
