    "story": "The machine gun spoke in short sentences. Short, because the gunner fed it that way — three rounds, a breath, three more — and the berm took the rest of the noise and gave it back as dust. GOLEM, the hull said, in white paint the crew had brushed on themselves. A name out of clay and old stories: a thing made to walk and guard. The gunner believed in the name more than he believed in the steel. Steel could be pierced. A name, once painted, stayed. The next burst was the word the tank had been saving. Somewhere beyond the berm, the field was listening. It did not answer.",
