    "story": "The men in the second tank counted the flame, once and then again in their heads, to be sure — men count anything that might one day be aimed at them. The flame belonged to the first tank, and the first tank's smoke went up in a white wall, thick enough to hide a whole crew's thinking. The second tank's gun was still loaded, still waiting, and its loader's hand hovered over the next round without taking it. Not yet.",
